## How to work

Stay scoped to this worktree. Don't modify other tickets. Decompose freely with subagents for depth, but don't add new scope (features, broad refactors, "while we're here" cleanups) — surface those instead. Before claiming a code change done, run it through whatever review/validation/test subagents your environment provides and fix what they find.

## Status

{{if eq .Status "in_progress"}}OpenKanban moved this ticket to in_progress on spawn. Don't change the status programmatically — the user moves it through in_review then done.{{else}}Ticket status is `{{.Status}}`. OpenKanban does not change ticket status on spawn — the user moves it through in_review then done.{{end}}

## When you're done

Use the **`finishing-an-openkanban-ticket`** skill to wrap up (NOT `superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch`). It verifies build/tests, self-evaluates readiness, then lands the work via one permission prompt (commit → PR → merge) and a reflective wind-down. Don't change ticket status to `in_review`/`done` yourself, and don't ask about deleting the branch/worktree — OpenKanban handles that on ticket delete. Follow your global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` for signing and push gates.{{end}}
